    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a narrowed focus, as limited availability forces us to rely on a lean offensive core. **Junior Caminero** remains our primary anchor at 57.19. While he faces Griffin, who boasts a respectable 3.88 xERA, **Junior Caminero** is elevated by his prime spot in the three-hole and current hot-hand metrics, which offset the slight drag created by the lefty-on-lefty matchup. **Christian Yelich** follows with a 52.38 score; while Yamamoto poses an elite challenge, the platoon advantage for **Christian Yelich** in the five-hole provides enough floor for a marginal start. Given our rigid adherence to game caps, we are playing it safe with this pair, ensuring we don't bleed efficiency against high-tier pitching.\n\nThe bench remains heavy with high-ceiling talent currently sidelined by scheduling gaps. We are particularly eager to get **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Caleb Durbin** back into the fold, as their combined speed profiles represent the backbone of our SB strategy\u2014the scarcest category in our 5x5 build. **Yordan Alvarez** was the most notable \"near miss\" for today, though his absence is purely situational due to a team off-day. With **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Colt Keith**, and **Lars Nootbaar** also resting, our depth is fully intact for the final stretch. We are monitoring **Hector Rodriguez**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** closely, as the rotation of these secondary pieces will be critical if the matchup volatility increases for **Junior Caminero** or **Christian Yelich** as the games progress.",
